University Leaders
(20)
It is the responsibility of each University Leader (e.g. Business Unit manager) to ensure that:
the policies and procedures for which they are responsible, are up to date and when they reference legislation, that they are regularly reviewed to ensure the legal information they contain is current (the Compliance team can assist as required);
their internal business processes embed and comply with the University’s compliance requirements;
compliance incidents/incidents are reported to the Compliance Manager as soon as practicable;
they engage in continuous improvement by reviewing the adequacy of controls and recommend/implement new ones as appropriate;
their staff are aware of and comply with the University’s compliance requirements, policies and procedures;
compliance responsibilities are included in position descriptions as appropriate; and
staff are encouraged to raise compliance concerns and participate in compliance training activities.
